UID:4ade31cf5d271a75858b1a1f797d59e3772026_10:26:59_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Monster Mash 2026: Camp Crystal Queer
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325253
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Friday, October 30th for the Yale LGBTQ Center’s annual Monster Mash as we head into the woods for Camp Crystal Queer—a retro summer-camp nightmare filled with ’80s slasher energy, eerie campfire legends, queer camp, and just enough mystery to make you question what’s moving on the other side of the lake.\n\nPicture moonlit cabins, flickering flashlights, neon windbreakers, feathered hair, suspiciously glamorous camp counselors, and stories whispered around the fire that always begin with, “They say it happened right here…” Come dressed in your best final-girl fantasy, doomed-counselor couture, scream-queen glamour, lake-creature realness, varsity-jock throwback, masked-menace look, or whatever you’d wear for one very strange last night at summer camp.\n\nExpect a playful collision of retro horror, spooky storytelling, queer excess, and Halloween fun as Camp Crystal Queer transforms Monster Mash into the kind of camp where the counselors are missing, the fire is getting low, and no one can quite explain the footsteps outside the cabin.\n\nStudents, faculty, staff, alumni, and their families are welcome.\n\nThe sun is setting. The stories are getting stranger. Somewhere in the woods, a branch just snapped.\n\nWelcome to Camp Crystal Queer. Check in, gather ’round the fire, and try to survive the night. 🔦🔥🔪\n\n💄 Show off your most creative, glamorous, frightening, or completely unhinged Halloween look\n\n👑 Compete in our annual Costume Contest\n\n🍬 Enjoy free food, decadent treats, and hauntingly good fun\n\n🎭 Explore themed activities and surprises throughout the Center\n\n🎶 Dance the night away at one of Yale’s favorite Halloween traditions\n\n🌈 Students, faculty, staff, alumni, and their families are all welcome.\n\nHelp Bring Monster Mash to Life! 🏳️‍🌈\n\nVolunteer opportunities will be available throughout the day for setup, decorating, activity hosting, event support, and cleanup. Whether you can help for an hour or stay for the entire evening, every contribution helps us create an incredible celebration for the community.\n\nVolunteer sign-up information coming soon.\n\n📍 Yale LGBTQ Center, 135 Prospect Street\n🕘 Starts at 9 PM\n\nCome dressed to impress, frighten, enchant, or surprise us—and prepare for the best Halloween party at Yale.\n\n#MonsterMash2026 #YaleLGBTQCenter #HalloweenAtYale #SpookySeason #YaleEvents #QueerJoy #VolunteerAtYale\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325253
END:VEVENT
