UID:f224b7d682e36c819d33c56320d85ec6772026_1:41:16_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Planting Possibilities 
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325298
DESCRIPTION:Planting Possibilities is a welcoming community space that invites students to come together, connect, and reflect on the seeds we plant for our futures. Join us at the Yale LGBTQ Center (135 Prospect St.) for an engaging succulent planting workshop where we'll explore themes of growth, resilience, authenticity, and cultivating success, both in our own lives and in the soil before us. Inspired by the many ways LGBTQ+ people and allies build community, nurture belonging, and thrive in spaces where they can be fully themselves, this program celebrates the beauty of growth in all its forms. Through meaningful conversation, creativity, and hands-on planting, participants will have the opportunity to cultivate something unique and beautiful while fostering connection in a supportive and inclusive environment. Whether you're seeking community, inspiration, or simply a moment to pause, reflect, and grow, we invite you to plant possibilities with us and watch them flourish together.\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325298
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261113T194447Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260708T182631Z
