CATEGORIES;X-CG-CATEGORY=event_tags:Food,Conversation,First Generation,LGBTQ 
DTSTART:20261208T233000Z
DTEND:20261209T013000Z
UID:4bdc375429b047414388ff071f41bcfe772026_2:25:56_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Cooking with Sandra: Seasoned with Pride
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325304
DESCRIPTION:Sandra's Cooking Class: Seasoned with Pride is a welcoming community gathering that celebrates the joy of food, culture, and connection. Join us at the Yale LGBTQ Center (135 Prospect St.) for an interactive cooking experience where students can come together to share stories, build relationships, and explore the ways food nourishes both body and community. Inspired by the spirit of chosen family and the traditions that bring us together, this program offers an affirming space to learn new recipes, exchange experiences, and create something meaningful alongside others. Whether you're a seasoned cook or stepping into the kitchen for the first time, we invite you to bring your curiosity, your appetite, and your authentic self as we cook, connect, and celebrate the many flavors that make our community unique, seasoned with pride.\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261113T194434Z
