DTSTART:20260826T140000Z
DTEND:20260826T160000Z
UID:489484d550d844f2792b06754d16b7bf772026_3:02:59_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Meet the Yale LGBTQ Center Peer Liaisons
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325307
DESCRIPTION:Starting at Yale can feel exciting, overwhelming, and everything in between. The Peer Liaison Program provides first-year Yale College students with an additional layer of mentorship, connection, and support as they transition into campus life—especially students from historically and systematically minoritized communities.\n\nPeer Liaisons, or PLs, are trained and caring upper-class student leaders affiliated with Yale’s residential colleges and cultural or community centers, including the Yale LGBTQ Center. Through individual support, community-building events, and helpful campus connections, PLs help first-year students find resources, build relationships, and develop a stronger sense of belonging at Yale.\n\nCome meet the Yale LGBTQ Center’s Peer Liaisons, learn more about the program, and discover how a PL can support you during your first year.\n\nFirst-year Yale College students are encouraged to request a Peer Liaison:\nhttps://college.yale.edu/communities/student-leadership/peer-liaisons\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325307
END:VEVENT
