UID:096deae1f8ae2477a0c80b307125f8847202026_11:08:35_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:LGBTQ+ Disability Hangout
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325585
DESCRIPTION:The Yale LGBTQ Center and Yale Disability Peer Mentor Program invite students to the LGBTQ+ Disability Hangout, a welcoming space for connection, conversation, and community.\n\nTogether, we’ll discuss the intersections of gender, sexuality, disability, and chronic illness at Yale while sharing a meal in a relaxed, affirming environment. Come hang out with us, meet new people, and build community across identities and experiences. RSVP to help us plan accordingly.\n\nDinner provided. All are welcome.\n\nTo support the accessibility of this disability- and chronic illness-centered gathering, masks are required except while actively eating or drinking. Masks will be available at the event. Please do not attend if you are experiencing symptoms of a respiratory illness. Thank you for helping us create a more accessible gathering.\n\nHosted by: \nJohanna Staples-Ager (johanna.staples-ager@yale.edu)\n\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2325585
END:VEVENT
