UID:d138e02db7fe67693150c67f0d0804538252026_1:19:00_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:An Afternoon with Schuyler Bailar
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2327040
DESCRIPTION:The Yale LGBTQ Center is amplifying this community event hosted by James Blackstone Memorial Library in Branford. Schuyler Bailar (he/him), educator, bestselling author, and inclusion advocate, will share his groundbreaking journey as the first transgender athlete to compete on an NCAA Division I men’s team in an engaging presentation and discussion. His books include He/She/They: How We Talk About Gender and Why It Matters and Obie Is Man Enough. Registration is required for this in-person event and closes Saturday, November 21 at 1:00 p.m. Hosted by James Blackstone Memorial Library. Sponsored by the John Loeb Lecture Fund.\n\nPlease register here through the library in addition to the Yale Connect: https://www.meetup.com/everyday-adventurers/events/316596636/\n\nIf you need transportation, please fill out this form: https://forms.gle/NZzQffBkhgeNUt2ZA\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2327040
END:VEVENT
