UID:be61672d66596ea8b7c39f99f1ef9f5b912026_2:23:04_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Pure and Impure Thoughts: A Homodoxy Seminar
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2328511
DESCRIPTION:Think queerly. Read deeply. Be in community.\n\nPure and Impure Thoughts is a monthly reading and discussion seminar from Homodoxy exploring theological, sexual, political, and social meanings of purity and impurity across religious traditions and genres—particularly as they relate to gay, queer, and trans lives and loves.\n\nConversation is informal, exploratory, and engaged, and readings vary in length and difficulty.\n\nFall 2026 readings:\nSeptember 9 — Indecent Theology: Theological Perversions in Sex, Gender, and Politics by Marcella Althaus-Reid\nOctober 14 — The Trouble with Normal: Sex, Politics, and the Ethics of Queer Life by Michael Warner\nNovember 11 — Reading to be announced\nDecember 9 — Reading to be announced\n\nThe seminar meets from 6:00–8:00 PM at the New Haven Pride Center, 50 Orange St., New Haven. Participation is free. Homodoxy notes that the readings and discussion are most appropriate for ages 18+.\n\nOrganized by Homodoxy and led by Yale alum Samuel Ernest, Ph.D. RSVP through Homodoxy to receive information about the readings.\n\nThe Yale LGBTQ Center is sharing this event on behalf of Homodoxy.\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2328511
END:VEVENT
